#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The max-cut problem {#the-max-cut-problem}"
msgstr "Masalah max-cut {#the-max-cut-problem}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The max-cut problem is a combinatorial optimization problem that is defined on a graph $G = (V, E)$, where $V$ is the set of vertices and $E$ is the set of edges. The goal is to partition the vertices into two sets, $S$ and $V \\setminus S$, such that the number of edges between the two sets is maximized.\n"
"For the detailed description of the max-cut problem, please refer to the [Quantum approximate optimization algorithm](/tutorials/quantum-approximate-optimization-algorithm) tutorial.\n"
"The max-cut problem is also used as an example in the [Advanced techniques for QAOA](/tutorials/advanced-techniques-for-qaoa) tutorial.\n"
"In those tutorials, the QAOA algorithm is used to solve the max-cut problem.\n"
msgstr ""
"Masalah max-cut adalah masalah optimasi kombinatorial yang didefinisikan pada graf $G = (V, E)$, di mana $V$ adalah himpunan simpul dan $E$ adalah himpunan sisi. Tujuannya adalah membagi simpul menjadi dua himpunan, $S$ dan $V \\setminus S$, sedemikian sehingga jumlah sisi antara kedua himpunan tersebut dimaksimalkan.\n"
"Untuk deskripsi lengkap masalah max-cut, silakan rujuk tutorial [Quantum approximate optimization algorithm](/tutorials/quantum-approximate-optimization-algorithm).\n"
"Masalah max-cut juga digunakan sebagai contoh dalam tutorial [Advanced techniques for QAOA](/tutorials/advanced-techniques-for-qaoa).\n"
"Dalam tutorial-tutorial tersebut, algoritma QAOA digunakan untuk menyelesaikan masalah max-cut.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Graph -> Hamiltonian {#graph-hamiltonian}"
msgstr "Graf -> Hamiltonian {#graph-hamiltonian}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Let us first consider a random graph with 100 nodes.\n"
msgstr ""
"Mari kita pertimbangkan terlebih dahulu sebuah graf acak dengan 100 "
"simpul.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/pauli-"
"correlation-encoding-for-qaoa/extracted-"
"outputs/37edb718-2bab-49d7-ad66-5f2f67d2aeff-0.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/pauli-"
"correlation-encoding-for-qaoa/extracted-"
"outputs/37edb718-2bab-49d7-ad66-5f2f67d2aeff-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We encode the graph with 100 nodes into two-body Pauli-matrix correlations "
"across nine qubits (see the explanation below). The graph is represented as "
"a correlation matrix, where each node is encoded by a Pauli string. The sign"
" of the expectation value of the Pauli string indicates the partition of the"
" node. For example, node 0 is encoded by a Pauli string, $\\prod_0 = I_{8} "
"\\otimes ... I_2 \\otimes X_1 \\otimes X_0$. The sign of the expectation "
"value of this Pauli string indicates the partition of node 0. We define a "
"*Pauli-correlation encoding* (PCE) relative to $\\prod$ as\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita mengkodekan graf dengan 100 simpul ke dalam korelasi matriks Pauli dua-"
"bodi pada sembilan qubit (lihat penjelasan di bawah). Graf direpresentasikan"
" sebagai matriks korelasi, di mana setiap simpul dikodekan oleh sebuah "
"string Pauli. Tanda nilai ekspektasi string Pauli menunjukkan partisi simpul"
" tersebut. Misalnya, simpul 0 dikodekan oleh string Pauli, $\\prod_0 = I_{8}"
" \\otimes ... I_2 \\otimes X_1 \\otimes X_0$. Tanda nilai ekspektasi string "
"Pauli ini menunjukkan partisi simpul 0. Kita mendefinisikan sebuah *Pauli-"
"correlation encoding* (PCE) relatif terhadap $\\prod$ sebagai\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$$ x_i \\coloneqq \\textit{sgn}(\\langle\\prod_i \\rangle), $$\n"
msgstr "$$ x_i \\coloneqq \\textit{sgn}(\\langle\\prod_i \\rangle), $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where $x_i$ is the partition of node $i$ and $\\langle \\prod_i \\rangle \\coloneqq  \\langle \\psi |\\prod_i| \\psi \\rangle $ is the expectation value of the Pauli string encoding node $i$ over a quantum state $|\\psi \\rangle$.\n"
"Now, let's encode the graph into a Hamiltonian using PCE.\n"
"We divide the nodes into three sets: $S_1$, $S_2$, and $S_3$.\n"
"Then, we encode the nodes in each set using the Pauli strings with $X$, $Y$, and $Z$, respectively.\n"
"We need to extract a relationship between the number of nodes and qubits that we will need to encode all the nodes. Using all possible permutations for the encoding yields to:\n"
msgstr ""
"di mana $x_i$ adalah partisi simpul $i$ dan $\\langle \\prod_i \\rangle \\coloneqq  \\langle \\psi |\\prod_i| \\psi \\rangle $ adalah nilai ekspektasi string Pauli yang mengkodekan simpul $i$ atas keadaan kuantum $|\\psi \\rangle$.\n"
"Sekarang, mari kita kodekan graf ke dalam Hamiltonian menggunakan PCE.\n"
"Kita membagi simpul menjadi tiga himpunan: $S_1$, $S_2$, dan $S_3$.\n"
"Kemudian, kita mengkodekan simpul-simpul di setiap himpunan menggunakan string Pauli dengan $X$, $Y$, dan $Z$, masing-masing.\n"
"Kita perlu mengekstrak hubungan antara jumlah simpul dan qubit yang dibutuhkan untuk mengkodekan semua simpul. Menggunakan semua permutasi yang mungkin untuk pengkodean menghasilkan:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"m=3\\binom{n}{k}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"m=3\\binom{n}{k}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "In this example we consider $k=2$, hence,\n"
msgstr "Dalam contoh ini kita menggunakan $k=2$, sehingga,\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"m  = \\frac{3}{2} n(n-1).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"m  = \\frac{3}{2} n(n-1).\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Therefore, the number of qubits $n$ needed to express a certain number of "
"nodes $m$ read as:\n"
msgstr ""
"Oleh karena itu, jumlah qubit $n$ yang dibutuhkan untuk mengekspresikan "
"sejumlah simpul $m$ adalah:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"n = \\left\\lceil \\frac{1 + \\sqrt{1 + \\tfrac{8}{3}m}}{2} \\right\\rceil.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"n = \\left\\lceil \\frac{1 + \\sqrt{1 + \\tfrac{8}{3}m}}{2} \\right\\rceil.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Note that the $\\lceil \\cdot \\rceil$ symbol represents the ceiling "
"function, which rounds any real number up to the next integer. This ensures "
"that the number of qubits is an integer.*\n"
msgstr ""
"*Perhatikan bahwa simbol $\\lceil \\cdot \\rceil$ mewakili fungsi ceiling, "
"yang membulatkan bilangan real apa pun ke atas ke bilangan bulat berikutnya."
" Ini memastikan bahwa jumlah qubit merupakan bilangan bulat.*\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Step 2: Optimize problem for quantum hardware execution {#step-2-optimize-"
"problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"
msgstr ""
"Langkah 2: Optimalkan masalah untuk eksekusi hardware quantum "
"{#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Quantum circuit {#quantum-circuit}"
msgstr "Quantum Circuit {#quantum-circuit}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here, the state $|\\psi \\rangle$ is parameterized with $\\mathbf{\\theta}$, and we optimize these parameters $\\mathbf{\\theta}$ using a variational approach.\n"
"This tutorial employs the `efficient_su2` ansatz for our variational algorithm due to its expressive capabilities and ease of implementation.\n"
"We also use the relaxed loss function, which will be introduced later in this tutorial.\n"
"As a result, we can address large-scale problems with fewer qubits and shallower circuit depths.\n"
msgstr ""
"Di sini, state $|\\psi \\rangle$ diparameterisasi dengan $\\mathbf{\\theta}$, dan kita mengoptimalkan parameter $\\mathbf{\\theta}$ ini menggunakan pendekatan variasional.\n"
"Tutorial ini menggunakan ansatz `efficient_su2` untuk algoritma variasional kita karena kemampuan ekspresifnya dan kemudahan implementasinya.\n"
"Kita juga menggunakan fungsi loss yang direlaksasi, yang akan diperkenalkan nanti dalam tutorial ini.\n"
"Hasilnya, kita bisa menangani masalah berskala besar dengan qubit yang lebih sedikit dan kedalaman Circuit yang lebih dangkal.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/pauli-"
"correlation-encoding-for-qaoa/extracted-"
"outputs/035f6b4a-4de0-452a-b60f-7260f9e3103a-0.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/pauli-"
"correlation-encoding-for-qaoa/extracted-"
"outputs/035f6b4a-4de0-452a-b60f-7260f9e3103a-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Loss function {#loss-function}"
msgstr "Fungsi Loss {#loss-function}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For the loss function $\\mathcal{L}$, we use a relaxation of the max-cut objective function as described in [\\[1\\]](#references), which is defined as $\\mathcal{V}(\\mathbf{x}) \\coloneqq \\sum_{(i, j) \\in E} W_{i, j}(1-x_i x_j)$. Here, $W_{i, j}$ denotes the weight of the edge $(i, j)$, and $x_i$ represents the partition of node $i$.\n"
"The loss function  $\\mathcal{L}$ is given by:\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk fungsi loss $\\mathcal{L}$, kita menggunakan relaksasi dari fungsi objektif max-cut sebagaimana dijelaskan dalam [\\[1\\]](#references), yang didefinisikan sebagai $\\mathcal{V}(\\mathbf{x}) \\coloneqq \\sum_{(i, j) \\in E} W_{i, j}(1-x_i x_j)$. Di sini, $W_{i, j}$ menunjukkan bobot dari sisi $(i, j)$, dan $x_i$ merepresentasikan partisi node $i$.\n"
"Fungsi loss $\\mathcal{L}$ diberikan oleh:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$\\mathcal{L}\\coloneqq \\sum_{(i, j) \\in E} W_{i, j} \\text{tanh} (\\alpha"
" \\langle\\prod_i \\rangle) \\text{tanh} (\\alpha \\langle\\prod_j \\rangle)"
" + \\mathcal{L}^{(\\text{reg})},$\n"
msgstr ""
"$\\mathcal{L}\\coloneqq \\sum_{(i, j) \\in E} W_{i, j} \\text{tanh} (\\alpha"
" \\langle\\prod_i \\rangle) \\text{tanh} (\\alpha \\langle\\prod_j \\rangle)"
" + \\mathcal{L}^{(\\text{reg})},$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where the max-cut objective function is replaced by the smooth hyperbolic "
"tangents of the expectation values of the Pauli strings encoding the nodes. "
"The regularization term $\\mathcal{L}^{(\\text{reg})}$ and the rescaling "
"factor $\\alpha$, proportional to the number of qubits, are introduced to "
"improve the solver's performance.\n"
msgstr ""
"di mana fungsi objektif max-cut digantikan oleh tangen hiperbolik yang mulus"
" dari nilai ekspektasi string Pauli yang mengenkode node-node tersebut. Suku"
" regularisasi $\\mathcal{L}^{(\\text{reg})}$ dan faktor penskalaan ulang "
"$\\alpha$, yang proporsional terhadap jumlah qubit, diperkenalkan untuk "
"meningkatkan performa solver.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The regularization term is defined as:\n"
msgstr "Suku regularisasi didefinisikan sebagai:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$\\mathcal{L}^{(\\text{reg})}$ is defined as $\\mathcal{L}^{(\\text{reg})} "
"\\coloneqq \\beta \\nu \\lbrack \\frac{1}{m} \\sum_{i \\in V} \\text{tanh} "
"(\\alpha \\langle\\prod_i \\rangle)^2 \\rbrack ^2$\n"
msgstr ""
"$\\mathcal{L}^{(\\text{reg})}$ didefinisikan sebagai "
"$\\mathcal{L}^{(\\text{reg})} \\coloneqq \\beta \\nu \\lbrack \\frac{1}{m} "
"\\sum_{i \\in V} \\text{tanh} (\\alpha \\langle\\prod_i \\rangle)^2 \\rbrack"
" ^2$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where $\\beta=1/2$, $\\nu = |E|/2 + (m -1) /4$, $|E|$ is the number of "
"edges, and $m$ is the number of nodes in the graph.\n"
msgstr ""
"di mana $\\beta=1/2$, $\\nu = |E|/2 + (m -1) /4$, $|E|$ adalah jumlah sisi, "
"dan $m$ adalah jumlah node dalam graph.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Step 3: Execute using Qiskit primitives {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-"
"primitives}"
msgstr ""
"Langkah 3: Eksekusi menggunakan Qiskit primitives {#step-3-execute-using-"
"qiskit-primitives}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this tutorial, we set `max_iter=50` in the optimization loop for "
"demonstration purposes. If we increase the number of iterations, we can "
"expect better results.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam tutorial ini, kita menetapkan `max_iter=50` dalam loop optimasi "
"sebagai tujuan demonstrasi. Jika kita meningkatkan jumlah iterasi, kita bisa"
" mengharapkan hasil yang lebih baik.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Step 4: Post-process and return result in desired classical format "
"{#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"
msgstr ""
"Langkah 4: Post-process dan kembalikan hasil dalam format klasik yang "
"diinginkan {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-"
"format}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The partitions of the nodes are determined by evaluating the sign of the "
"expectation values of the Pauli strings that encode the nodes.\n"
msgstr ""
"Partisi node-node ditentukan dengan mengevaluasi tanda dari nilai ekspektasi"
" string Pauli yang mengenkode node-node tersebut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can calculate the cut size of the max-cut problem using the partitions of"
" the node.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita bisa menghitung ukuran potongan dari masalah max-cut menggunakan "
"partisi node.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Once the training is complete, we perform one round of single-bit swap search to improve the solution as a classical post-processing step.\n"
"In this process, we swap the partitions of two nodes and evaluate the cut size. If the cut size is improved, we keep the swap. We repeat this process for all possible pairs of nodes connected by an edge.\n"
msgstr ""
"Setelah pelatihan selesai, kita melakukan satu putaran pencarian swap satu-bit untuk memperbaiki solusi sebagai langkah post-processing klasik.\n"
"Dalam proses ini, kita menukar partisi dua node dan mengevaluasi ukuran potongan. Jika ukuran potongan meningkat, kita menyimpan pertukaran tersebut. Kita mengulangi proses ini untuk semua pasangan node yang terhubung oleh sebuah sisi.\n"

